<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bingo Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bingo Province was an old province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> on the Inland Sea, now the eastern part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiroshima-prefecture">Hiroshima Prefecture</a>. With neighbouring Aki it was held by the Mōri clan until 1600 and then by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fukushima-masanori">Fukushima Masanori</a>. After 1619 its western part belonged to the Asano of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiroshima">Hiroshima</a> and its eastern part to the Fukuyama domain.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bingo-province.jpg" alt="Bingo Province" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ash_Crow · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Provinces_of_Japan-Bingo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
